{"timestamp": "2026-07-03T08:19:05.613995+00:00", "user_id": "anonymous", "layer": "output_validator", "blocked": false, "query": "How do I apply for a mortgage?", "response": "Here are the steps to apply for a mortgage:\n\n1. Research and compare lenders: Start by researching different mortgage lenders to find the best rates and terms that suit your needs. You can check online platforms, visit local banks, or consult with a mortgage broker.\n\n2. Gather necessary documents: Most lenders require certain documents to process your mortgage application. These typically include proof of income, tax returns, bank statements, identification, and details about the property you intend to purchase. Make sure to gather all the required documents beforehand to streamline the application process.\n\n3. Pre-approval: Consider getting pre-approved for a mortgage to determine the loan amount you qualify for. This will help you set a realistic budget and strengthen your position when making an offer on a property.\n\n4. Complete the application: Once you have chosen a lender, you will need to fill out a mortgage application form. This form will ask for your personal information, employment details, financial history, and information about the property.\n\n5. Submit the application: After completing the application form, submit it to the lender along with the required documents. Some lenders may provide an online application portal for convenience.\n\n6. Review and sign the offer: If your mortgage application is approved, the lender will provide you with an offer, including the loan amount, interest rate, and repayment terms. Review the offer carefully and make sure you understand all the details before signing it.\n\n7. Property appraisal and underwriting: The lender will typically conduct a property appraisal to ensure the value aligns with the loan amount. They will also perform underwriting, which involves verifying your financial information and assessing the risk associated with lending to you.\n\n8. Closing the mortgage: If the property appraisal and underwriting are successful, the closing process will begin. This involves signing the final loan documents, paying any applicable fees, and transferring ownership of the property.", "reason": "Pydantic validator passed", "latency_ms": 6976.85, "metadata": {"source": "rag", "category": "Mortgage Application", "confidence": 0.95}}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-03T08:19:07.504382+00:00", "user_id": "anonymous", "layer": "success", "blocked": false, "query": "How do I apply for a mortgage?", "response": "Here are the steps to apply for a mortgage:\n\n1. Research and compare lenders: Start by researching different mortgage lenders to find the best rates and terms that suit your needs. You can check online platforms, visit local banks, or consult with a mortgage broker.\n\n2. Gather necessary documents: Most lenders require certain documents to process your mortgage application. These typically include proof of income, tax returns, bank statements, identification, and details about the property you intend to purchase. Make sure to gather all the required documents beforehand to streamline the application process.\n\n3. Pre-approval: Consider getting pre-approved for a mortgage to determine the loan amount you qualify for. This will help you set a realistic budget and strengthen your position when making an offer on a property.\n\n4. Complete the application: Once you have chosen a lender, you will need to fill out a mortgage application form. This form will ask for your personal information, employment details, financial history, and information about the property.\n\n5. Submit the application: After completing the application form, submit it to the lender along with the required documents. Some lenders may provide an online application portal for convenience.\n\n6. Review and sign the offer: If your mortgage application is approved, the lender will provide you with an offer, including the loan amount, interest rate, and repayment terms. Review the offer carefully and make sure you understand all the details before signing it.\n\n7. Property appraisal and underwriting: The lender will typically conduct a property appraisal to ensure the value aligns with the loan amount. They will also perform underwriting, which involves verifying your financial information and assessing the risk associated with lending to you.\n\n8. Closing the mortgage: If the property appraisal and underwriting are successful, the closing process will begin. This involves signing the final loan documents, paying any applicable fees, and transferring ownership of the property.", "reason": "All guardrails passed", "latency_ms": 9448.29, "metadata": {"source": "rag", "category": "Mortgage Application", "confidence": 0.95, "rag_context": "Thank you for your interest in applying for a mortgage! I'd be happy to guide you through the process. Here are the steps to apply for a mortgage:\n\n1. Research and compare lenders: Start by researching different mortgage lenders to find the best rates and terms that suit your needs. You can check online platforms, visit local banks, or consult with a mortgage broker.\n\n2. Gather necessary documents: Most lenders require certain documents to process your mortgage application. These typically include proof of income, tax returns, bank statements, identification, and details about the property you intend to purchase. Make sure to gather all the required documents beforehand to streamline the application process.\n\n3. Pre-approval: Consider getting pre-approved for a mortgage to determine the loan amount you qualify for. This will help you set a realistic budget and strengthen your position when making an offer on a property.\n\n4. Complete the application: Once you have chosen a lender, you will need to fill out a mortgage application form. This form will ask for your personal information, employment details, financial history, and information about the property.\n\n5. Submit the application: After completing the application form, submit it to the lender along with the required documents. Some lenders may provide an online application portal for convenience.\n\n6. Review and sign the offer: If your mortgage application is approved, the lender will provide you with an offer, including the loan amount, interest rate, and repayment terms. Review the offer carefully and make sure you understand all the details before signing it.\n\n7. Property appraisal and underwriting: The lender will typically conduct a property appraisal to ensure the value aligns with the loan amount. They will also perform underwriting, which involves verifying your financial information and assessing the risk associated with lending to you.\n\n8. Closing the mortgage: If the property appraisal and underwriting are successful, the closing process will begin. This involves signing the final loan documents, paying any applicable fees, and transferring ownership of the property.\n\nRemember, each lender may have specific requirements and processes, so it's essential to communicate directly with them for any additional instructions or clarifications. Best of luck with your mortgage application, and feel free to reach out if you have any further questions!", "stage_latency_ms": {"input_guardrail": 0.08, "rag_search": 192.99, "rag_rerank": 351.36, "rag_total": 578.0, "agent_llm": 6976.85, "llm_judge": 1891.9, "total": 9448.29}}}
